-- title:
--   Igusa Gauss ring at ∞ cuts out the constant reduction (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q=2$, a nonzero $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $(q:\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ a nonunit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (the subfield of Laurent series over the residue field $\kappa$ of $A$ generated by `jqModC` and `jqNModC`) whose members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, i.e. the rational affine geometric places at which the value of the geometric $j$-generator lies in `ssJSet`. Let `hle` witness $F_0 :=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` $\le F :=$ `fieldBar q M'` inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series, and let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $A$ on $F_0$ with reduced field `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F_0$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the reduced field with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A \to \kappa$, together with a degree-preserving map on places satisfying the divisor-pushforward rule. Assume (`hR₀`) that every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series lies in $F_0$ is $R_0$-integral with $R_0$-residue the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Fix a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ (an element of `Idx q`), a family $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $F$ indexed by the projective line over $\mathbb{Z}/q$, and a family $O^{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$. Assume: $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ consists exactly of the quotients $x/y$ of $A$-coefficient Laurent series with $\bar y \neq 0$ (in the sense that $f \cdot y = x$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series and the reduction of $y$ is nonzero); each $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ is the pullback of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ carrying $\infty$ to $\ell$ under `redQ`; $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective and permuted by pullback along every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; each $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ meets $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ exactly in $A$, is fixed by those pullbacks, contains an element $t$ with $t - a$ a unit for every $a \in A$, and dominates $R_0$ in the sense that any $R_0$-integral $f$ which is regular wherever the image of `jq` is regular and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$ maps into $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, with $f - a$ in the maximal ideal whenever the residue of $a \in A$ equals the value of the $R_0$-residue of $f$ at $s$. The conclusion: for every $f \in F_0$, $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if the image of $f$ in $F$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$.
--
--   This is the $q$-expansion principle for the Gauss (Igusa) valuation ring at the cusp $\infty$: it identifies the level-$M'$ constant reduction attached to $A$ with the restriction to $F_0$ of the Igusa chart at infinity, in the case $q=2$. It feeds the construction of the semistable covering of the full-level modular curve, being used in the analysis of the Igusa-component charts and their descent (maximal ideals, rational places, smoothness of the two-chart integral model).
